    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68314,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 246,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A primary thymic carcinoma with both squamous and glandular differentiation in which each component constitutes &ge;&nbsp;10% of the tumour within a resection specimen</li>\r\n<li>Exclusion of mucoepidermoid carcinoma</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The squamous component should be positive for p63/40 and/or CK5/6</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-22T17:00:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68315,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 246,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "<p>Adenosquamous carcinoma of the thymus should be staged according to the TNM system [[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM classification of malignant tumours. 8th ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]] {25396314} and, optionally, the Masaoka&ndash;Koga system {21847052}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-14T11:08:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
